    rdf:value """him goodbye. Called on Mrs. Rogers etc. in the afternoon, and dined with old Miss Norton alone - very pleasant, but B.B. ill.
Thursday Feb. 25. 04.
Whistler again, and dear Mr. Freer. Mr. Fox came to lunch, and took us to call on a jolly sick widow, Mrs. Nickerson. Then he carried B.B. off to see Dr.
Langmaid, who discovered enlarged turbindles in the poor man’s nose. We dined with Mrs. Whitman. I sat by the nearly inarticulate Mr. Dove.
Friday Feb. 26. 04 
Bernhard in bed. I went to museum and argued with that silly Potter about that obviously school picture called “Veronese”. He had not seen the most important of Paolo’s works, yet he argued as if he knew all about it. Billy Taylor was there. Power and Fox and Billy Taylor went to see Bernhard in bed. I """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 187 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1903-04> .

